# "Sybaritic - A Spartan protocol library for Python"

Now that Rogallo[i] supports multiple protocols[ii], it’s tempting to add one or two more. As of the time of writing, alongside Gemini[iii], both Gopher[iv] and Finger[v] are supported. While wandering the small web[vi], I stumbled on the Spartan protocol[vii]. Given its similarity to Gemini and the fact it uses Gemtext[viii] as its main document type, adding it to Rogallo seemed like an obvious thing to do.

=> https://rogallo.davep.dev/ [i]
=> https://rogallo.davep.dev/protocols/ [ii]
=> https://rogallo.davep.dev/gemini/ [iii]
=> https://rogallo.davep.dev/gopher/ [iv]
=> https://rogallo.davep.dev/finger/ [v]
=> https://blog.davep.org/tag/smolweb/ [vi]
=> https://github.com/michael-lazar/spartan [vii]
=> https://blog.davep.org/tag/gemtext/ [viii]

In aid of this, I’ve created Sybaritic[i]. It is, in effect, a sibling library to Wasat[ii], Port70[iii] and Port79[iv].  As with the others, it is async-all-the-way and is designed to have a similar API.

=> https://sybaritic.davep.dev/ [i]
=> https://wasat.davep.dev/ [ii]
=> https://port70.davep.dev/ [iii]
=> https://port79.davep.dev/ [iv]

With this in place, I can now extend Rogallo to handle spartan:// URIs as first-class citizens.

